never replaces its identity (Table 7); there the attacker does not hide among the newcomers but
stays old, and, once past its own priority window, is audited only from what the priority phase and
newest-first targeting leave. Lemma 2 does not cover such an attacker, since it bounds the audits of
a replacement identity. Where the selected attack does replace (3 markets at p = 0.05), R3 audits
between 0.041 and 0.095 of its jobs. The measured share falls at each of the four sampled rates; four
